<section id="page-rules" class="page rules-page" hidden><div class="page-intro"><span class="eyebrow">READ THIS. PRETEND YOU DIDN’T.</span><h1>FIGHT DIRTY.<br>PLAY SMART.</h1><p>Three to six fighters. Ten points of self-esteem. Six terrible choices.</p></div><div class="rules-layout"><div><section class="panel rule-block"><span class="rule-number">01</span><h2>Everybody goes at once.</h2><p>Pick your move and, when needed, another fighter. Nobody sees your choice until the turn resolves. You can change your mind before the timer runs out. Miss a turn and lose 1 self-esteem.</p></section><section class="panel rule-block"><span class="rule-number">02</span><h2>Survive the nonsense.</h2><p>At zero self-esteem, you’re out. When only one or two fighters remain, they win. Yes, two survivors can share the victory. Making temporary friends is a strategy. Keeping them is optional. If a fight reaches the turn limit, the fighters with the most self-esteem share the win.</p></section><section class="panel rule-block"><span class="rule-number">03</span><h2>Earn your place.</h2><p>Every completed ranked fight updates ratings and records. Winners earn 10 points plus 20 per defeated opponent; other finishers earn 10. Running away earns no points. The bots use these same rules.</p></section></div><div class="panel move-reference"><h2>YOUR SIX DIRTY TRICKS</h2><dl><dt>SCRATCH</dt><dd>Deal 1 damage, or 2 if the target is grabbed or trying to lick a lolly.</dd><dt>GRAB</dt><dd>Interrupt scratching, grabbing, teasing or licking. The first grab holds; extra grabs deal 1 damage each.</dd><dt>TEASE</dt><dd>One teaser does nothing. Two or more successful teasers deal 2 damage each. Coordinate, then cackle.</dd><dt>COWER</dt><dd>Block one grab or scratch, plus all tattle damage. Multiple attackers can still hurt you. Repeated unproductive cowering costs self-esteem.</dd><dt>LICK A LOLLY</dt><dd>Use one of your three lollies to restore 2 self-esteem, maximum 10. Grabs and scratches interrupt it. Successful licking blocks tattle damage.</dd><dt>TATTLE</dt><dd>You get two. One tattler deals 3 damage to unprotected opponents. If two or more tattle together, the tattlers take 3 damage instead.</dd></dl><p class="tiny muted">Actions resolve in classic order: cower, grab, lick setup, scratch/tease, tattle. A lolly can’t revive a fighter already knocked out.</p></div></div><div class="panel rule-credits"><h2>OLD-SCHOOL SOUL. NXT CHAPTER.</h2><p>Sissy Fights NXT is a PHP/MySQL remaster of SiSSYFiGHT 2000. Original code © 2015 Ranjit Bhatnagar, Naomi Clark and Eric Zimmerman (MIT). Original artwork, music and sound are licensed under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CC BY 4.0</a>. Original art/interface: Jason Mohr; art direction: Yoshi Sodeoka; revival visual design: Cindi Geeze and Terry Wiley; music/sound: Lem Jay Ignacio. All 32 fighter looks and ten new arenas have been illustrated for this NXT edition. Original music and sound by Lem Jay Ignacio return from <a href="https://github.com/moonmilk/sissyfight" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the official open-source SiSSYFiGHT release</a>; audio is enabled by default and begins when your browser permits playback after an interaction. Your sound and volume choices are remembered. New interface and illustrations created for Sissy Fights NXT.</p><p class="tiny">The playground is fictional. The rivalry stays in the game. Bots are clearly labelled. No purchases, no external accounts, no downloads required to play.</p></div></section>
